# Polylane PR merge gate

When a PR has the GitHub label **`polylane`** (check via `gh pr view <n> --json labels` / PR page), **do not merge** until the user explicitly agrees after the briefing below.

## Before merge (required)

In Russian, briefly cover all three points — no wall of text:

1. **Суть** — в чём заключается PR (что меняется в коде / зависимостях / инфре).
2. **Влияние на бота** — как это затронет работу бота в проде (рантайм, UX, деплой, риск регрессий).
3. **Практическая необходимость** — зачем это реально нужно сейчас (не «потому что Dependabot/линтер сказал»), и что будет, если не мержить.

Then **stop and wait** for an explicit yes / «мержи» / equivalent. Silence, «ок, понял», or review-only replies are **not** consent to merge.

## After merge or close (required)

When a `polylane` PR is **merged** or **closed without merge**, also close the **source Polylane Issue** that produced the PR. Do not leave the Issue open after the PR is done.

1. **Find the Issue** — from the PR body / deliverable badge (`console.polylane.com/.../deliverables/...` or `console.polylane.com/issues/iss_…`), Polylane MCP, or the admin DM that announced the Issue. Also close any GitHub issues listed in `closingIssuesReferences` / `Fixes #N` if still open.
2. **Close it** — via Polylane MCP if available; otherwise Console / documented API. Confirm status is no longer `new` / open.
3. **Close without merge** — leave a short PR comment explaining why (Polylane reads it for the next fix), then close the source Issue the same way (wontfix / obsolete / duplicate — whatever matches).
4. **Report** — tell the user the PR outcome and that the Issue is closed (with Issue URL/id). If the Issue cannot be closed (MCP/auth down), say so and ask them to close it in Console — do not treat the PR as fully finished.

## Do not

- Merge a `polylane` PR without that Russian briefing **and** explicit user approval
- Treat auto-merge, squash-on-green, or «usual Dependabot merge» as a bypass
- Skip the briefing because the change looks small or «safe»
- Merge or close a `polylane` PR and leave its Polylane Issue open
- Skip the «why» comment when closing a `polylane` PR without merging
